      "content": "According to standard HACCP guidelines, cooked poultry must be cooled from 135°F to 70°F within 2 hours and from 70°F to 41°F within a total of 4 hours to mitigate Clostridium perfringens risks. This cooling process should involve breaking up large masses to increase surface area for faster heat transfer. Failure to adhere to these specific temperatures and time limits creates a \"danger zone\" where bacteria can multiply rapidly before they are killed by reheating or inhibited by acidic environments.",
